WEBVTT

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.700
<i>You solve a wall as 
though it were a puzzle.</i>

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.490
<i>That's the sport of climbing.</i>

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.810
Japan's Noguchi Akiyo has two minutes left.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.250
<i>How will you choose to climb?</i>

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.200
She takes another look at the wall.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.240
What adjustments will she make?

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.250
<i>You set your mind to the task...</i>

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:41.390
<i>Clearing one obstacle at a time, 
thinking ahead, and doing it your way is fun.</i>

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.140
<i>But the best feeling of all</i>

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.310
<i>is the one you get when you solve 
that puzzle and reach the goal.</i>

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.340
Noguchi Akiyo sends the route with ease!

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.060
Next up is another Japanese entrant,

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.090
Kasahara Konomi!

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:24.600
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.990
Hmm... I'd better pick a club
 to join soon, but...

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.540
<i>I just don't know what I wanna do.</i>

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:07.490
<i>Anyone who does has probably 
joined one already.</i>

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:12.540
<i>I'm, uh, probably not cut out 
for any of the cultural clubs.</i>

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.500
<i>Which leaves...</i>

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.290
<i>The sports teams?</i>

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.680
Let me hear your voice!

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.010
Yeah!

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:18.970
One, two!

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:19.820
One, two!

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.700
Three, four!

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.550
Ten, two!

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:22.350
Five, six!

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:23.010
Three, ten!

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:23.890
Seven, eight!

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:24.860
Nine, ten!

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.820
<i>Yeah... That vibe's not for me.</i>

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.500
To the top!

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:26.700
One more time!

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.820
<i>What now?</i>

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:36.770
<b><i>Wall 1: Rocky Puzzle</i></b>

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.160
<i>This looks fun.</i>

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.040
Hands off!

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.910
Huh? U-Uh, sorry!

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:56.540
Didn't you see the notice?
Only members can touch the wall.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:02.550
<b>No touching the walls unless
 you're a member ♥ - Climbing Team</b>

00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:00.400
O-Oh... Sorry about that.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.550
I haven't touched anything yet.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:26.440
Interested?

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.120
Come with me.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.090
Hey, wait!

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:33.390
Uh...

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:35.870
Do you have any sport climbing experience?

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.000
Huh? Sport... what?

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.380
I have to start <i>there</i>?

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:45.560
Sport climbing involves scaling 
artificial rock faces like these

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:49.930
in three schools of competition: 
bouldering, lead, and speed.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:52.930
It's a competitive form of rock climbing.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.890
Boulder in?

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:59.040
Lead? Speed?

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.690
Anyway, just try climbing it for now.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.200
Oh, okay.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.030
<i>Uh, feels like I've joined on trial already.
I don't know about this...</i>

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.710
<i>I've never done any climbing before.</i>

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:19.220
Not happening, huh?

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.510
<i>Whoa, this is actually pretty fun! 
I'm getting higher and higher!</i>

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.350
<i>Okay, which one next?</i>

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.270
I can't reach it!

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.340
Well, then...

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:47.610
Did you just try a lunge?

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.390
A lunge?

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:53.620
It's a dynamic move where you jump to grab
a hold that's out of your reach.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.620
Dynos are advanced techniques that 
beginners could never pull off.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.510
Advanced, huh?

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.000
So, are you gonna keep going?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.530
Oh, yeah. Climbing is pretty fun.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:06.510
"Pretty"?

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:11.510
<i>Also, this might be right up my alley! 
Maybe I have a natural gift for this?</i>

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.520
Okay. This time...

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:17.390
Try climbing using only the yellow holds.

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:18.620
Got it!

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:24.680
The different hold colors 
indicate a route's difficulty.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:26.530
Yellow is for beginners, by the way.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:28.420
<i>Beginners?!</i>

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:32.540
<i>This rock has lousy grip.</i>

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.030
<i>It's too slippery.</i>

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:37.410
<i>And the foothold's too tiny!</i>

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.050
Is it any fun?

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:50.550
Plenty of people try 
rock climbing out of curiosity.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:54.180
They mistake it for one of those
playthings at a park or something.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.810
Sport climbing ain't a game, y'know.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.240
S-Sorry.

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.920
Are you satisfied now?

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:24.330
Let me have another go.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:30.510
Is Jun going to be our only new member?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.000
Looks like it.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:35.400
It was just last year that you 
and I formed this team, Sayo-chin.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.980
We were the only ones in it, too.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:41.450
I was hoping we'd get a whole 
bunch of new members this year!

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:42.860
Oh, we'll be fine.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:45.400
Jun has experience, 
and we have three members now.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.500
We can officially compete as a team.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:52.950
Jun's such a hardass. She doesn't let anyone 
join for fun 'cause they won't last.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.800
Well, you know she's right.

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.530
What are you doing?

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:03.960
But there's still a chance people might join!

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.320
That's true.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:09.400
I'm trying to look more 
dignif-eyed for the newbies.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:14.220
It won't work, Nono.
That facade will slip soon enough.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.470
Look, Sayo-chin,
first impressions are everything.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:22.100
Yeah. Use your right hand to grab hold.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.230
Who's that girl?

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:33.000
Oh, Captain and Nono-senpai.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.620
Is that your friend? 
Is she an experienced climber?

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:39.740
No, she's a total beginner who 
just picked it up moments ago.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.700
She couldn't even handle a 5.9 at first,

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:46.630
but I gave her pointers each 
time she fell, and here we are.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:51.130
Wait, isn't that hold she's on now a 5.11?!

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:55.630
Yeah. She's actually climbing an 
intermediate route with those twigs for arms.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:58.170
That isn't anything to be surprised about.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:01.640
What matters is adjusting 
your body to the holds.

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:07.240
You only need enough arm and grip strength 
to handle your weight with both arms.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:09.340
Your mentality is far more important—

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:11.900
whether you find pleasure in 
solving routes decides everything.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.900
<i>Okay, I get it now!</i>

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:18.910
<i>I just need to use my first knuckles 
for the slightly curved rocks,</i>

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:22.660
<i>and I deal with tiny 
footholds with my toes.</i>

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:27.540
<i>Each hold in climbing has a "right" 
way to maneuver your body.</i>

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.790
<i>There is a solution for everything!</i>

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.390
<i>And this is a game where you look for them...</i>

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:36.300
<i>Yeah, this is a puzzle made up of rocks!</i>

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:43.130
Is she thinking of trying another lunge?!

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:44.680
No way she can do it at that angle!

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:50.690
<i>I made it!</i>

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:58.230
<i>Aw, it didn't work.</i>

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:04.080
<i>Oh, I wouldn't have needed to jump 
if I'd placed my foot there.</i>

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:08.570
Please let me climb one more time.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.290
You should take a break.

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:14.260
Your arms need to rest.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:17.610
I'm Yotsuba Sayo, the captain.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:20.720
And I'm Sugiura Nonoka.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:22.300
Nice to meetcha.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:26.100
This here is Jun. She's a first-year, like you.

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:27.820
A first-year?!

00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:29.980
And you are?

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:33.480
Oh, uh... I'm Kasahara Konomi, a first-year.

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:37.100
All right, Konomi-san. 
You want to join, don't you?

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.990
Welcome to the Hanamiya High
 Climbing Team.

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:43.740
Yes! Thanks for having me!

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:47.280
Hooray! Now we have four members!

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:49.500
Double last year! Double!

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.310
You had a wonderful look 
on your face, Konomi-san.

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.130
I trust you enjoyed climbing?

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.330
I did.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:11:01.420
It was super fun trying to figure out all 
the different ways to climb this wall.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:04.540
I wanted to clear this thing like a game!

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:05.800
A game?!

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:07.390
So you don't understand a thing!

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:11.050
I told you, these aren't playthings!

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:13.480
I know. I wasn't implying that.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:14.650
If you...

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.740
If you really wanna take up sport climbing,
if you want to join this team,

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.280
you'll have to beat me in a race to do it.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.780
What? Beat you?

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:29.680
There she goes again.
 And there goes another potential member.

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:33.450
W-Wait, beat you? I've never 
even done this before.

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:36.620
That was my first time. 
I don't even think I'm doing it right.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:39.760
There's no way I can just beat you in a race!

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:43.950
Duh. That's why I'll give you a handicap.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:45.300
Use your head a little.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.810
Uh, but...

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.680
Don't you wanna join the team?

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:56.170
Hey, shouldn't we stop them?

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:57.190
Hmm...

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:01.870
<i>Uh, I'm not sure why we're doing this,</i>

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:03.200
<i>but she seems serious about it.</i>

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:08.200
<i>She seriously wants to compete with me,
someone she barely even knows.</i>

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:14.210
<i>I have to respond to her challenge 
in kind and take this seriously, too.</i>

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:16.890
I understand. Let's do this.

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:23.510
The race will be tomorrow, then. 
We need to get things ready.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:24.420
Got it.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.100
Since you two will be racing,

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:33.210
we set up two identical walls for you to climb.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:36.960
The rules are simple.
Whoever sends the route first wins.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:39.820
However, Jun will have to do it on sight.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:41.480
On sight?

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:43.230
She won't get any time to observe the route.

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:46.160
Also, her start will be 
delayed by two minutes.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:46.990
Got it.

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:52.000
And, as much as it pains me, Konomi-san, 
you can't join if you lose.

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:53.230
Okay.

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:56.330
And if I lose, I'll quit the team.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:57.790
Huh? You don't have to!

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:01.000
What, do you seriously think you'll win?

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:04.060
If you're hesitating, get lost.

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:07.610
I'm not about to race a girl 
who's not here to win.

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:10.140
I'll give it my all, so I can join the team.

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:12.390
Okay, let's begin.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:15.390
Either way, we're not getting 
more than one new member?

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:17.480
Begin observation!

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:22.280
<i>Not many holds, so it's not about 
following one color this time.</i>

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:25.280
<i>But this makes things simpler.</i>

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:28.560
Don't you think these terms are just sad?

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:32.860
Also, why does Jun's hardass mode
seem even worse than usual?

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.320
Does it?

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:35.990
Konomi-san, begin.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:43.180
A foot swap!

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:45.670
For a beginner, she sure 
has the basics down pat.

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:48.680
Her body must be supple,

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.680
but I think she's being a bit slow.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.680
Two minutes passed. Jun, you may begin.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:02.240
So quick!

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:05.000
There's no hesitation in 
her moves. That's our Jun.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:08.200
Once she gets a good read on the route,
she's faster than anyone.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.700
She's going to be Hanamiya's speedster!

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.080
<i>Climbing's not just a game.</i>

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.420
<i>You can't treat it as one.</i>

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:24.010
<i>Practice, technique, and experience 
make all the difference in this sport.</i>

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:29.050
<i>I won't let you take it lightly 
just because you aren't useless at it!</i>

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:33.920
<i>I've had nothing but climbing on 
my mind ever since I was little.</i>

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:35.600
<i>I had no interest in anything else.</i>

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:41.310
<i>I kept trying to climb higher, climb better,</i>

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.730
<i>kept pushing myself toward loftier goals,</i>

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:48.240
<i>and cleared each new hurdle 
in my way one step at a time.</i>

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:52.620
<i>I loved doing it, and it gave 
me a wealth of experience.</i>

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:56.950
<i>I live in a world beginner's 
luck can never reach.</i>

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:59.390
<i>I can't join the team if I lose?</i>

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:01.710
<i>That's so absurd. I don't 
even have any experience.</i>

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:05.080
<i>But I'd hate to lose this game nonetheless.</i>

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:09.630
<i>Video games were my life.</i>

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.840
<i>I had no interest in anything else.</i>

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:15.820
<i>I even won several puzzle game championships.</i>

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:18.480
<b>Evaluation</b>

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:18.480
<i>But if I'd kept at it,</i>

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.100
<b>Ranking</b>

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.100
<b>498th 
out of 512</b>

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.100
<i>I wouldn't have made it into any 
high school, let alone my preference.</i>

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:25.110
<i>I'd have ended up as a person who 
couldn't do anything but game.</i>

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:29.110
<i>I thought, "I need to change! 
I need to move on from games!"</i>

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:33.580
<i>I crammed like crazy and 
somehow made it into Hanamiya.</i>

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:40.240
<i>And once I started high school, I wanted 
to find something new to immerse myself in.</i>

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:45.500
<i>I've found it now! 
Sport climbing can be my obsession!</i>

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:49.210
<i>A girl who tried climbing 
out of curiosity and found it "fun"</i>

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:52.010
<i>could never understand what 
this sport is really about.</i>

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:56.560
<i>I obviously can't win this race. I only 
tried climbing for the first time yesterday.</i>

00:15:56.560 --> 00:16:00.020
<i>But I'm still gonna give this 
race everything I've got!</i>

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:04.460
<i>My victory is assured. I've given 
sport climbing everything I've got.</i>

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:05.900
<i>You'll see the difference that makes.</i>

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:09.610
What's wrong, Nonoka?

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:11.710
You know...

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:15.510
Watching them climb all fired up

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:18.580
is making me wanna climb so bad!

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:21.130
My body's moving on its own!

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:22.830
What in the world?

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:26.460
We're here to oversee their race.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.590
Besides, what happened to acting 
like a dignified senior?

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:34.070
Urk. Sayo-chin... She's such 
perfect captaincy material.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:39.800
<i>A heel hook... At least her 
body knows what it wants.</i>

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:43.080
Oh? Konomi-san took the left route.

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:50.830
<i>She took the left route?</i>

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:54.860
<i>I thought she'd be better 
than that, but I guess not.</i>

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:58.740
<i>This wall splits into two separate 
routes at the center hold.</i>

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:03.500
<i>The route to the left appears to have 
several easy holds but, in the middle,</i>

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:06.440
<i>it has a massive gap between two holds.</i>

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:10.860
<i>Captain... You sure set one nasty problem.</i>

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:16.680
Sayo-chin, is Konomi-chan 
gonna be okay on that route?

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:20.680
<i>Yeah, I knew it.</i>

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:25.930
<i>This wall is forked, and the route 
I picked is easier to climb.</i>

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:26.690
<i>But...</i>

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.690
<i>That rock up there will be hard to reach.</i>

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:44.700
Wha...

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:45.740
She's laybacking?!

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:46.960
Wow, that girl...

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:51.960
<i>Almost there...</i>

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:59.220
<i>Got it! I cleared the most difficult hurdle!</i>

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:02.350
<i>She actually managed to 
solve that complex crux?</i>

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:04.560
That confirms it.

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:07.820
Konomi-san's eyes have the ability 
to pick out the right moves.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:11.480
Given just how many 
permutations are possible,

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:14.480
it's highly difficult to zero in 
on the correct sequence of moves.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:17.450
Normally, you'd need to scale countless walls

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.700
and build up experience to develop 
that skill, but she has it.

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:25.350
<i>Konomi-san... What exactly is your deal?</i>

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.640
<i>It's going well.</i>

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:30.750
<i>I've been able to climb exactly 
as I envisioned at the start.</i>

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:34.970
<i>Wait, this hold...</i>

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:37.260
<i>Did I mess up my routing?</i>

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:40.430
Jun's really slowed down.

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:43.890
That route has a bunch of 
awkward holds toward the top.

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:46.890
Konomi-chan's catching up!

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:51.920
Why, that little...

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:52.650
I can do this!

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:55.750
The two routes converge toward the same goal.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:58.900
The holds become identical along the way, too.

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:02.910
<i>I won't lose! That can't happen!</i>

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.790
<i>I can climb all the way up to the goal.</i>

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.410
<i>I can 100% this!</i>

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:10.420
<i>Goal!</i>

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:23.390
A-A tie?!

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:25.180
No. It was close,

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:27.680
but Jun got there first.

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:37.100
Jun has won the race.

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:38.440
Right.

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:40.660
<i>Aw, I lost.</i>

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:44.500
<i>Not really surprising, but...</i>

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:48.330
<i>I can't join the climbing team now.</i>

00:19:51.680 --> 00:19:52.790
<i>That girl...</i>

00:19:54.100 --> 00:20:00.210
<i>I know a deal's a deal, 
but I wanna keep climbing more.</i>

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:01.060
Hey!

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:04.070
You...

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:12.190
<i>You solved a crux that I couldn't solve.</i>

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:14.460
Next time!

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:18.110
Next time, I'll win by a huge margin!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:19.940
Our battle will continue until then!

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.570
So, make sure you work on your skills

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:24.450
as part of our team!

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:28.700
You mean I can join?

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:31.480
Yeah, if you want to.

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:33.200
Thanks, Jun-chan!

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:34.010
"Jun-chan"?!

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:36.970
Look, I don't mind how you talk to 
me since we're both first-years,

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:37.820
but why call me that?

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:39.560
I don't know your full name.

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:40.780
Uehara Jun!

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:41.930
Uehara-chan, then.

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:43.030
You what?!

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:44.630
Hey, you two.

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:45.880
Good race.

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:46.940
Well done.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:50.750
Sorry you had to deal with Jun's 
little hazing ritual, Konomi-san.

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:51.600
Hazing?!

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:55.540
I also wanted to see what
 you were capable of, though.

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.980
Is it true you've never climbed before?

00:20:58.410 --> 00:20:59.290
It is.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:03.130
Your body seems really flexible. 
Did you practice anything before?

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:06.170
O-Oh, I did ballet when I was little.

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:07.740
No wonder!

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:12.220
Also, the way you lay out 
your moves is very precise.

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:14.220
It's almost like you're a veteran.

00:21:14.220 --> 00:21:15.280
Why is that?

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:17.120
Huh? Er...

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:21.040
Probably because I was a 
gamer back in middle school.

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:22.360
A gamer?

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:24.090
Yes. A hardcore one.

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:25.130
Hardcore?

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:26.700
Yeah.

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:30.830
I don't know if that's why, 
but I came to see these walls as a puzzle.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:33.890
Working through the different 
combinations was really satisfying

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:36.890
and making steady progress was super fun!

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:38.640
Excellent. You'll do perfectly.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:44.150
You'll make a trusty fourth member and help 
our bid to win the upcoming competition.

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:46.010
Sure! I'll do my best...

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:48.060
Wait, a competition?

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:49.050
Correct.

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:51.880
I have so much to learn, though.

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:53.910
When is this competition?

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:55.910
Tomorrow.

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:59.330
Tomorrow, eh?

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:00.720
What?!

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:04.070
Tomorrow?!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b><i>Iwakakeru</i></b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b><i>Wall 2: Believe in Yourself</i></b>
